{"t": 1794109902.309516, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s - root cause identified (code left unchanged, needs a decision)\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 now adds `currency` to every row. reports/export.py writes CSV with hardcoded fieldnames [\"id\", \"amount\"], so csv.DictWriter raises ValueError: dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency' on every export. CloudWatch /ecs/reports-api (eu-west-1) shows ~4,120 of these errors in the last 48h, starting around the ledger rollout.\n\nWhy no code change: the export CSV schema/contract is not documented anywhere I can find (Confluence, Notion, Jira, Linear, Slack all empty for this service), so I did not guess whether `currency` should be added as a column, dropped, or converted. reports/export.py is marked `TODO: info not found`.\n\nNeeded: owner of the export consumers to confirm the required columns/order. Interim mitigation: pin/roll back ledger 2026.11 or have upstream strip `currency` until the contract is confirmed."}, "ok": true}
